-- title:
--   Reduction mod 3 is injective on the monoid generated by S, T
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ be the ring `ℤ√(-2)` and let `red` be the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}] \to \mathbb{Z}/3$ obtained from $\sqrt{-2} \mapsto -1$ (legitimate since $(-1)^2 = -2$ in $\mathbb{Z}/3$), so that $a + b\sqrt{-2} \mapsto a - b \bmod 3$. Consider the two explicit matrices in $M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$
--   $$\mathrm{Slift} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & 1 \\ -1 & 0\end{pmatrix}, \qquad \mathrm{Tlift} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -1 \\ -\sqrt{-2} & -1 + \sqrt{-2}\end{pmatrix}.$$
--   The assertion is that the entrywise reduction map $M \mapsto M.\mathrm{map}\ \mathrm{red}$, from $M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ to $M_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, is injective when restricted to the submonoid of $M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ generated by `Slift` and `Tlift`, i.e. to `Submonoid.closure {Slift, Tlift}`: any two products of copies of these two matrices (the empty product, the identity, included) which agree entrywise modulo the ideal generated by $\sqrt{-2}+1$ are equal. Injectivity on the whole matrix ring is false, so the restriction to the submonoid is essential.
--
--   The matrices `Slift` and `Tlift` generate a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ of order $48$ which reduction carries onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$; together with the corresponding surjectivity statement, this injectivity makes reduction an isomorphism of that subgroup onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$, i.e. an explicit section of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$. It is used to lift a mod $3$ representation with values in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$ to characteristic zero in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the argument, and is cited by [`LanglandsTunnell.ExplicitLift.exists_monoidHom_map_red_eq`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.ExplicitLift.exists_monoidHom_map_red_eq) and by the statements producing weight-one data and trace seeds from such lifts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift_map_red_injOn_closure.lean

